quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  63,5,"And when it is said to them: ‘Come! So Allah’s Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) may seek forgiveness for you,’ they turn their heads aside (rudely), and you see them turning away in arrogance."
  63,6,"It makes no difference for them whether you seek forgiveness for them or do not seek forgiveness for them: Allah will never forgive them (for they mock you and behave arrogantly towards you). Indeed, Allah does not guide the rebellious people."
  63,7,"They are the ones who say: ‘Do not spend (anything) on those who remain (as devotees) in the presence of the Messenger of Allah until they break away (from him).’ And to Allah belong the treasures of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand."
  63,8,"They say: ‘If we return to Medina, then (we) the honourable will surely expel the dishonourable (i.e. the Muslims) from it.’ But all honour belongs to Allah, His Messenger and the believers. However, the hypocrites do not understand."
  63,9,"O believers! Do not let your possessions or your children divert you from the remembrance of Allah. For whoever does that, it is they who are the losers."
  63,10,"Spend (in charity) from whatever We have provided you before death comes upon one of you, and he says: ‘O my Lord! If only You would grant me respite for a while so I could give charity and be among the righteous?’"
  63,11,Allah shall never grant respite to a soul when its appointed time (of death) has arrived. And Allah is All-Aware of what you do.
